    },
    "message": "Compute different Runs at once in the server\n\nProjectAPI kept one job for the whole server. It now keeps one job per\nRun, as the Run's writer lease allows, and the server accepts up to\nmax_jobs Runs at once, each in its own process (--max-parallel-runs,\ndefault 2). A Run with a job still refuses a second computation, a fork\nand deletion; another Run forks, computes and cancels on its own. The\nthread worker of tests and the CLI keeps one job, since threads share\nthe GIL.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
